I've had a look at this and its definitely a bug, but its a not quite what I thought you had described.<br><br>What appears to be happening, is if the scanning holds on a channel its not calculating the distance to that repeater, its displaying the last distance that was calculated to a repeater<br><br>e.g. If you start on Channel 1 and its distance is 10.5km  and then start scanning.  When the scan holds on a channel because of a signal, the distance that is displayed to that Channel is show as 10.5km even if the distance to the repeater is not 10.5km,  i.e its using the cached distance<br><br>I will investigate and fix this problem<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Sat Dec 21, 2024 8:46 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
