Am I crazy, or in the past was it possible to see the repeater distance when you hit the P2 (SK1) button when the option to display the distance in the settings was set to off? I used to have the display distance set to off since the most of the zones had names which encroached on the ability to display the distance, so I'd just hit P2 to see how far away the repeater was if I was interested.<br><br>I also noticed that when scanning, with display distance turned on, the radio stops for a transmission and shows "--" for distance unless you stop the scan, then the distance immediately appears. I unfortunately don't recall if this is a new phenomenon or if it's always been that way, but I figured I mention it just in case it was new and unintentional.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=3765">KB0PCH</a> — Mon Dec 16, 2024 6:08 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
